  "uses exact owned root ledger transaction APIs and canonical event sequence",
  "closes ledger inspection and owned roots in finally without masking failures",
  "builds one branded snapshot per reopen and reuses it across evaluator query and citations",
  "uses the lower named foundation line kind-file and transaction byte ceilings on reopen",
  "keeps run data and local documents out of repository and package contents",
  "rebuilds identical scholarly decisions from reconstructed records and requests",
  "reconstructs legacy V1 records unchanged while prospective evaluation fails closed",
  "keeps historical revision closure valid and rejects stale refs introduced by latest records",
  "rejects omitted and duplicate reconstructed requests without mutating the run",
  "audits canonical URL duplicate and strong-identifier ambiguity after reopen",
